<%# locals: totals - CollectionStats::ProxyCards %>
<div class="p-6 border rounded-3xl bg-foreground border-highlight">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-5">
    <%= render partial: 'collection_stats/kpi', locals: {
      label: 'Proxy Copies', value: number_with_delimiter(totals[:copies]),
      sub: 'cards you printed' } %>

    <%= render partial: 'collection_stats/kpi', locals: {
      label: 'Printings', value: number_with_delimiter(totals[:printings]),
      sub: 'rows on this page' } %>

    <%#
      The one that decides what this page is for. Everything else is inventory; this is the count of
      proxies with nothing real behind them anywhere.
    %>

    <%= render partial: 'collection_stats/kpi', locals: {
      label: 'Proxy Only', tone: :accent, value: number_with_delimiter(totals[:proxy_only]),
      sub: 'no real copy anywhere' } %>

    <%= render partial: 'collection_stats/kpi', locals: {
      label: 'Notional Value', value: number_to_currency(totals[:value]),
      sub: 'what the pile would cost for real' } %>

    <%= render partial: 'collection_stats/kpi', locals: {
      label: 'Cost to Replace', value: number_to_currency(totals[:cost_to_replace]),
      sub: 'the proxy-only ones' } %>
  </div>

  <%#
    Said plainly because it contradicts the rest of the app on purpose: no other page prices a proxy,
    for the reason CollectionStats::Sql spells out. Here the notional number IS the question.
  %>

  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-grey-text/50">
    Proxies carry no value anywhere else in the app - these two figures are what the pile would cost
    to buy for real, and they are counted nowhere but here.
  </p>
</div>
